  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They didn't fold after the lead slipped away in the fourth.",
    "what_this_means": "Late-game execution is becoming the only consistency this roster has. Devers supplied the power. Two runs in crucial moments. But the broader story was a team that trailed after five innings and found it again in the seventh. That's not resilience as identity yet; it's a survival reflex. They left runners scattered through the middle innings, converted just six of twenty-two RISP situations, and still pulled ahead when it mattered most. The bullpen held clean after McDonald exited: Gage, Winn, and Brubaker combined for three and two-thirds scoreless. This is what fragile looks like. Winning by the margin they create, not the depth they possess. One more one-run win. That margin is eroding faster than it holds.",
